WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.234
Digital footprints are discovered through lawful review of public sources.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:08.368
Search engines can locate indexed pages, documents, profiles, and references.

00:00:08.368 --> 00:00:12.915
Public records and official websites can establish dates, ownership claims, policies,

00:00:12.915 --> 00:00:14.155
or organizational relationships.

00:00:14.155 --> 00:00:17.876
Social platforms may show public statements and professional context,

00:00:17.876 --> 00:00:20.356
but identity and authenticity require validation.

00:00:20.356 --> 00:00:23.663
Archives can preserve prior versions of public pages.

00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:24.490
Domain, DNS,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:29.864
and certificate sources can help defenders reconcile their public infrastructure with internal inventories.

00:00:29.864 --> 00:00:33.171
Public code search can reveal organizational projects, references,

00:00:33.171 --> 00:00:36.892
or accidental exposure in repositories that are legitimately accessible.

00:00:36.892 --> 00:00:41.026
Image and metadata review can provide context about published material.

00:00:41.026 --> 00:00:45.160
These activities should serve an authorized defensive or analytical purpose,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.053
not identification or tracking of private individuals.

00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:53.841
Public breach notifications can help users and organizations understand that a provider reported exposure.

00:00:53.841 --> 00:00:58.801
Notifications are context for defensive account protection; they do not authorize obtaining,

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:02.522
trading, or using stolen data, passwords, or private records.

00:01:02.522 --> 00:01:05.002
Discovery should be documented and bounded.

00:01:05.002 --> 00:01:07.896
Record the purpose, source, date, and relevance.

00:01:07.896 --> 00:01:12.030
Avoid collecting unrelated personal details, entering private spaces, impersonating users,

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.270
or circumventing restrictions.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:18.231
If access requires a control you are not authorized to use, stop.

00:01:18.231 --> 00:01:21.951
Multiple discovery methods may surface the same underlying source.

00:01:21.951 --> 00:01:26.912
Trace claims to origin and do not mistake repeated indexing for corroboration.

00:01:26.912 --> 00:01:32.286
The useful outcome is a validated exposure finding with enough context for remediation,

00:01:32.286 --> 00:01:36.420
not a large collection of unverified personal or technical data.
